WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
The practice of turning bioethics into
enforceable law is a relatively modern

2
00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.680
invention, born entirely out of historical
necessity.

3
00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:13.300
This timeline tracks global standards for
medical research, beginning after

4
00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:19.100
the Second World War. It starts with the
1947 Code of Nuremberg and 1964

5
00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:22.600
Declaration of Helsinki, protecting human
subjects.

6
00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:27.600
Later, the architecture adapted to
genetics through the CIOMS and UNESCO

7
00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:31.860
declarations. While global standards
create a moral baseline,

8
00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:36.100
this chart illustrates how Europe built a
uniquely stringent dual-engine

9
00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:37.800
regulatory architecture.
